{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "13", "m": "11", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "02", "M": "18", "S": "41"}}, "news": [{"title": "Odisha RERA grants four-month relief to housing projects hit by West Asia conflict", "para": "Odisha Real Estate Regulatory Authority has announced a four-month extension for project timelines affected by the West Asia conflict. This decision follows an advisory from the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs regarding project completion dates. Promoters are not required to pay any fees to obtain this extension. Registered projects with completion dates on or after February 28, 2026, qualify for this relief.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/rera/odisha-rera-grants-four-month-relief-to-housing-projects-hit-by-west-asia-conflict/135770955?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-345562/135770955.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "rera"}, {"title": "Spain approves housing measures after huge protests", "para": "In response to widespread public unrest and a significant general strike, Spain's interim lower house of parliament has officially approved housing reforms aimed at limiting evictions and controlling real estate speculation. These measures are set against the backdrop of upcoming national elections on November 29, where the opposition, led by the Popular Party, has signalled intentions to repeal such reforms if they come to power.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/international/spain-approves-housing-measures-after-huge-protests/135770417?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-205330/135770417.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "international"}, {"title": "Unitech's net loss widens to \u20b9808 crore in Q2 FY27", "para": "Unitech Ltd has reported a consolidated net loss of Rs 808.45 crore for the quarter ending September, alongside a total income drop to Rs 120.94 crore compared to last year. Facing severe cash flow issues, the company has seen project delays, especially in Delhi-NCR, affecting 20,000 customers eager for their homes. Financial troubles have prompted government intervention and a complete board restructuring.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/unitechs-net-loss-widens-to-808-crore-in-q2-fy27/135765226?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-169176/135765226.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}]}